      "id": "dbd7fcd4-fc3e-4906-86d0-f82760313f47",
      "name": "Get Existing Roster Rows1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [
        -1584,
        1056
      ],
      "alwaysOutputData": true,
      "credentials": {
        "googleSheetsOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "REDACTED",
          "name": "Google Sheets account"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Pulls the whole roster so the Code node can (a) compute next client_id and (b) check for an existing slug match, both in one pass. Fine at this volume; would not scale past a few thousand rows without a smarter lookup."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Canonical-record logic: compute next client_id, build the deterministic\n// name transformation, and flag a possible duplicate \u2014 all in one place so\n// there is exactly ONE spot in the whole workflow where the name is decided.\n\nconst form = $('Webhook - Client Signed1').first().json.body;\nconst existingRows = items.map(i => i.json);\n\nconst legalNameRaw = (form.legal_name || '').trim();\n\n// Strip trailing legal suffixes (Inc, Corp, Corporation, LLC, Co, Ltd),\n// tolerating an optional comma or space before the suffix and an optional\n// trailing period. Anchored with $ so it only strips a TRAILING suffix,\n// never one that happens to appear mid-name (e.g. \"Corp Solutions Inc\").\nconst suffixPattern = /[\\s,]*\\b(inc\\.?|corp(oration)?\\.?|llc\\.?|co\\.?|ltd\\.?)\\.?\\s*$/i;\n\nconst displayName = legalNameRaw.replace(suffixPattern, '').trim();\n\nconst slug = displayName\n  .toLowerCase()\n  .replace(/[^a-z0-9\\s-]/g, '')   // strip anything not alphanumeric/space/hyphen\n  .trim()\n  .replace(/\\s+/g, '-');          // collapse spaces to single hyphens\n\n// Next client_id = 1 + max existing id (first client ever gets 1)\nconst maxId = existingRows.reduce((max, row) => {\n  const id = parseInt(row.client_id, 10);\n  return isNaN(id) ? max : Math.max(max, id);\n}, 0);\nconst nextId = maxId + 1;\n\n// Duplicate check: does a row with this slug already exist?\nconst duplicateMatch = existingRows.find(row => row.slug === slug);\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    client_id: nextId,\n    legal_name: legalNameRaw,\n    display_name: displayName,\n    slug: slug,\n    primary_contact_email: form.primary_contact_email || '',\n    account_owner: form.account_owner || '',\n    is_duplicate: !!duplicateMatch,\n    duplicate_of_client_id: duplicateMatch ? duplicateMatch.client_id : null,\n    created_at: new Date().toISOString()\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "2624fab6-393c-499a-b88b-0bbb4d7dff6c",
      "name": "Compute ID + Canonicalize Name1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -1360,
        1056
      ],
      "notes": "The whole naming-mismatch fix lives here. Test this against 4-5 real-looking client names (with commas, 'LLC.', 'Ltd', etc.) before recording \u2014 verify the output by hand, don't trust it blind."
    },
